@page "/projects"

<PageTitle>Projects | Elaisa Baquir</PageTitle>

<section class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Projects</p>
    <h1>Student projects that show my progress in IT.</h1>
    <p>
        These projects represent the type of work I am learning to build as a 2nd year BSIT
        student. They focus on practical systems, clean layouts, and beginner-friendly code.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="project-grid">
    <article class="project-card">
        <div class="project-tag">Web Design</div>
        <h2>Personal Portfolio Website</h2>
        <p>
            A clean portfolio made with Blazor to introduce myself, organize my information,
            and present my student projects in a professional way.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Responsive black and pink interface</li>
            <li>Simple navigation and hover effects</li>
            <li>Home, About, Projects, and Contact pages</li>
        </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="project-card">
        <div class="project-tag">Database</div>
        <h2>Student Information System Concept</h2>
        <p>
            A school activity concept for storing student records, subjects, and basic
            enrollment details using organized database tables.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Entity planning and table relationships</li>
            <li>Basic CRUD workflow idea</li>
            <li>Focus on accurate and readable records</li>
        </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="project-card">
        <div class="project-tag">Programming</div>
        <h2>Simple Calculator Program</h2>
        <p>
            A beginner programming project that practices input handling, arithmetic
            operations, and clear output formatting.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Uses conditional logic</li>
            <li>Handles common operations</li>
            <li>Strengthens programming fundamentals</li>
        </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="project-card">
        <div class="project-tag">System Design</div>
        <h2>Library Borrowing Tracker</h2>
        <p>
            A proposed mini system for tracking borrowed books, return dates, and borrower
            information for a small school library.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Book and borrower records</li>
            <li>Borrow and return status</li>
            <li>Simple dashboard concept</li>
        </ul>
    </article>
</section>
